# Line-ending and diff policy.
#
# Deliberately surgical. `core.autocrlf=true` is set globally on the build
# machine and neither this repo nor hiddify-core had a .gitattributes, which is
# why some upstream-authored files report enormous churn that is entirely CRLF:
# hiddify-core/v2/hcore/grpc_server.go diffs as 296/300 but is 3/7 under
# `--ignore-cr-at-eol`.
#
# That is NOT fixed here. Adding `* text=auto` and renormalizing would rewrite a
# large share of the tree, destroy `git blame` on every affected file and
# permanently distort the fork-vs-upstream diff shape -- for four files. The
# merge/cherry-pick side is handled by `merge.renormalize=true` instead, which
# fixes conflicts without touching the index. See docs/upstream/METHODOLOGY.md.
#
# What follows only governs files whose content format actually matters.

# Rule-set binaries. Git's heuristic already detects these, but new .srs files
# arriving via `make fetch-rulesets` must never be line-ending converted -- the
# Go core mmaps them and the extractor verifies a sha256 from MANIFEST.
*.srs binary

# Generated by scripts/regen_rulesets_manifest.sh (bash, LF). Pinning the
# checkout to LF keeps the file byte-stable across regeneration on Windows.
assets/rulesets/MANIFEST text eol=lf

# Shell scripts are executed by Git Bash and WSL; CRLF breaks the shebang.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The upstream-sync ledgers are read with cut/comm/join/awk; a trailing CR would
# contaminate the last field. See docs/upstream/METHODOLOGY.md.
*.tsv text eol=lf
